00:20:01,536 --> 00:20:06,040
June, I really am.
All this bloodshed.

260
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:08,075
It's exactly
what I was trying to avoid.

261
00:20:08,075 --> 00:20:12,647
All those soldiers are dead.
You fucking slaughtered them.

262
00:20:12,647 --> 00:20:17,485
<i>- They invaded my country.</i>
- To save our children.

263
00:20:17,485 --> 00:20:20,988
- Citizens of Gilead.
- They were stolen from us.

264
00:20:20,988 --> 00:20:22,123
You knew that.

265
00:20:22,123 --> 00:20:25,326
<i>I gave you the chance
to be with Hannah.</i>

266
00:20:25,326 --> 00:20:27,595
You threw your lot in
with the Americans.

267
00:20:27,595 --> 00:20:29,430
Is that why you called?
To blame me?

268
00:20:29,430 --> 00:20:33,601
No. I called because
I want you to know

269
00:20:33,601 --> 00:20:35,503
you can still come
to New Bethlehem.

270
00:20:35,503 --> 00:20:37,471
Why would you let me do that?

271
00:20:38,172 --> 00:20:41,843
<i>Hannah's a symbol now.</i>

272
00:20:41,843 --> 00:20:44,712
<i>And like it or not, so are you.</i>

273
00:20:44,712 --> 00:20:49,350
So after last night,
it would be even more effective

274
00:20:49,350 --> 00:20:53,287
if June Osborne chose
to return to Gilead

275
00:20:53,287 --> 00:20:55,256
to be close to her child.

276
00:20:55,256 --> 00:20:58,560
You can be close to Nick too.

277
00:21:01,495 --> 00:21:04,165
- What do you mean?
<i>- Nick will be there.</i>

278
00:21:05,399 --> 00:21:06,634
<i>You could be neighbors.</i>

279
00:21:06,634 --> 00:21:09,771
<i>You could borrow
cups of sugar from each other,</i>

280
00:21:09,771 --> 00:21:12,273
whatever the kids
are calling it these days.

281
00:21:12,273 --> 00:21:15,777
Do you think that you can
just dangle Nick in front of me

282
00:21:15,777 --> 00:21:17,745
and I'll just do whatever
the fuck you want?

283
00:21:17,745 --> 00:21:21,215
I think it's a good deal
and I think you should take it.

284
00:21:28,923 --> 00:21:29,857
<i>But...</i>

285
00:21:32,426 --> 00:21:34,128
there's this one thing.

286
00:21:34,128 --> 00:21:36,463
Um...

287
00:21:36,463 --> 00:21:39,066
<i>I need you to go public.</i>

288
00:21:40,935 --> 00:21:45,807
Call the failed mission
a foolish act of aggression.

289
00:21:46,841 --> 00:21:50,311
What? No,
I'm not gonna say that.

290
00:21:50,311 --> 00:21:51,713
<i>Why not? It's the truth.</i>

291
00:21:51,713 --> 00:21:54,315
Americans did
what they always do.

292
00:21:54,315 --> 00:21:55,583
They put Hannah...

293
00:21:55,583 --> 00:21:59,486
They put all of those girls
in real danger.

294
00:21:59,486 --> 00:22:04,291
I cannot make Gilead
look like the victim here.

295
00:22:04,291 --> 00:22:10,364
Joseph, this is an...
It is an evil fucking country.

296
00:22:10,364 --> 00:22:12,867
- I can't do that.
- I'm trying to fix it

297
00:22:12,867 --> 00:22:16,370
- from the inside.
<i>- You are still a part of it.</i>

298
00:22:16,370 --> 00:22:18,039
You're one of them.

299
00:22:19,907 --> 00:22:23,177
It's even worse,
'cause I know you know better.

300
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:28,683
I'm doing what I can.

301
00:22:28,683 --> 00:22:31,953
Step by step
is what I promised Eleanor.

302
00:22:36,523 --> 00:22:37,825
Eleanor hated you.

303
00:22:41,528 --> 00:22:43,297
She couldn't stand
the sight of you.

304
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:50,738
She was so broken and so...

305
00:22:52,439 --> 00:22:53,908
<i>ashamed.</i>

306
00:22:56,744 --> 00:23:00,748
<i>By the man that she loved.</i>

307
00:23:04,518 --> 00:23:06,253
But she'd rather be dead.

308
00:23:13,294 --> 00:23:14,696
I watched her die.

309
00:23:19,633 --> 00:23:21,168
I did. I watched her die.

310
00:23:23,270 --> 00:23:24,872
<i>And I did nothing.</i>

311
00:23:26,507 --> 00:23:27,408
<i>Nothing.</i>

312
00:23:34,648 --> 00:23:36,083
I knew you had...

313
00:23:39,653 --> 00:23:41,122
something to do with it.

314
00:23:47,929 --> 00:23:50,698
But Eleanor would still want me
to help you with Hannah.

315
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:54,702
<i>Help come back.</i>

316
00:23:54,702 --> 00:23:56,704
I want her here.

317
00:24:00,441 --> 00:24:02,109
I want my baby here.

318
00:24:06,013 --> 00:24:07,048
Safe...

319
00:24:09,183 --> 00:24:10,251
and free.

320
00:24:13,988 --> 00:24:15,022
Please.

321
00:24:17,491 --> 00:24:18,926
It's never gonna happen.

322
00:24:25,566 --> 00:24:27,334
Then go fuck yourself.

323
00:24:48,089 --> 00:24:49,090
Fuck!

324
00:25:00,701 --> 00:25:01,969
Don't.

325
00:25:10,344 --> 00:25:13,347
I know. I know.

326
00:25:15,983 --> 00:25:17,885
- I know.
- Let me go.

327
00:25:17,885 --> 00:25:19,186
It's gonna be okay.

328
00:25:20,721 --> 00:25:23,324
- Please let me go.
- You're gonna be okay.

329
00:25:25,793 --> 00:25:26,994
You're gonna be okay.

330
00:25:30,464 --> 00:25:31,398
You're gonna be okay.

331
00:25:38,906 --> 00:25:40,307
We're gonna get her.

332
00:25:41,843 --> 00:25:44,211
Wait till they see him,
Mrs. Waterford.

333
00:25:44,211 --> 00:25:46,447
So pleased Mr. Wheeler
gave you permission.

334
00:25:46,814 --> 00:25:47,882
Me too.

335
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,388
Blessed day, Mrs. Wheeler.

336
00:26:02,930 --> 00:26:06,067
Stay away from my husband.

337
00:26:08,635 --> 00:26:11,906
Sneaking down all alone
in the middle of the night?

338
00:26:11,906 --> 00:26:14,942
- Mrs. Wheeler, I assure you--
- After I told you no?

339
00:26:15,742 --> 00:26:17,544
Who do you think you are?

340
00:26:20,915 --> 00:26:24,218
I am Mrs. Fredrick Waterford.

341
00:26:25,853 --> 00:26:27,354
To me you're just a whore.

342
00:26:33,060 --> 00:26:34,228
I'm coming with you.

343
00:26:36,363 --> 00:26:37,431
Get in.

344
00:27:19,073 --> 00:27:21,075
We shouldn't have trusted
those sources.

345
00:27:23,344 --> 00:27:26,047
Gilead was always one step
ahead of us, Mark.

346
00:27:33,754 --> 00:27:35,522
Lawrence called me this morning.

347
00:27:40,928 --> 00:27:42,663
I'm so done
with that son of a bitch.

348
00:27:46,767 --> 00:27:48,735
No doubt they see this
as a victory.

349
00:27:48,735 --> 00:27:50,171
Yeah.

350
00:27:53,740 --> 00:27:57,078
Fuck them. Fuck them, Mark.

351
00:28:01,415 --> 00:28:02,849
You know how
we honor those soldiers?

352
00:28:02,849 --> 00:28:05,286
We do not stop fighting.

353
00:28:05,286 --> 00:28:07,554
No matter what they throw at us,
we don't stop.

354
00:28:08,255 --> 00:28:09,656
Not for one fucking second.

355
00:28:11,758 --> 00:28:12,693
So what's next?

356
00:28:16,964 --> 00:28:18,165
What do we do now?

357
00:28:22,970 --> 00:28:25,272
- So you're done with Lawrence?
- Mmm-hmm.

358
00:28:26,140 --> 00:28:27,975
What about Nick Blaine?

359
00:28:30,744 --> 00:28:31,678
What about him?

360
00:28:32,646 --> 00:28:35,682
I offered to help him
when I was in Gilead,

361
00:28:36,883 --> 00:28:39,520
if he'd help us,
but he turned me down.

362
00:28:48,395 --> 00:28:53,100
What, to be your inside man
in Gilead or something?

363
00:28:53,100 --> 00:28:58,372
At first, but then, eventually,
to be our man here.

364
00:28:59,573 --> 00:29:00,507
With immunity.

365
00:29:04,578 --> 00:29:05,546
He said no?

366
00:29:06,980 --> 00:29:09,416
Yes, but he can still have that.

367
00:29:11,185 --> 00:29:12,719
Maybe you could persuade him.

368
00:29:17,158 --> 00:29:19,660
Nick was an Eye.
He's a Commander now.

369
00:29:19,660 --> 00:29:24,031
Someone like that defecting
from Gilead... Big impact.

370
00:29:28,735 --> 00:29:29,736
You can make one too.

371
00:29:35,542 --> 00:29:38,011
You could. You know that.

372
00:29:38,011 --> 00:29:40,481
After Angels' Flight,
after your testimony

373
00:29:40,481 --> 00:29:43,184
against Waterford,
you should step up.

374
00:29:43,984 --> 00:29:45,386
Put your power to use.

375
00:29:48,089 --> 00:29:50,657
I don't feel comfortable
doing that right now, Mark.

376
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:55,096
Fair enough.

377
00:29:57,698 --> 00:29:58,665
What about Nick?

378
00:30:01,535 --> 00:30:05,306
I could set up a meeting.
I could set it up today.

379
00:30:09,310 --> 00:30:10,711
Be nice to have a win.

380
00:30:13,046 --> 00:30:14,148
Yeah.

381
00:30:18,719 --> 00:30:19,653
Yeah, set it up.

382
00:30:28,203 --> 00:30:31,372
- Praise the Lord.
- Such a precious miracle.

383
00:30:31,372 --> 00:30:34,542
- So darling. You're so blessed.
- Thank you.

384
00:30:34,542 --> 00:30:37,245
My late husband and I,
God rest his soul,

385
00:30:37,245 --> 00:30:39,647
we tried for many years
to conceive.

386
00:30:39,647 --> 00:30:42,917
There was a lot of heartache
and disappointment.

387
00:30:42,917 --> 00:30:45,253
So I do understand
the yearning for a child.

388
00:30:45,253 --> 00:30:46,921
But Gilead helped a lot.

389
00:30:46,921 --> 00:30:50,425
Clean water, clean air,

390
00:30:50,425 --> 00:30:53,161
scrubbing all of those horrible
toxins out of the environment,

391
00:30:53,161 --> 00:30:56,464
and above all,
a devotion to God.

392
00:30:56,464 --> 00:30:58,599
And living by
the highest of moral standards.

393
00:30:58,599 --> 00:31:02,036
So, you follow Gilead's path
in Toronto,

394
00:31:02,036 --> 00:31:03,404
then perhaps you too

395
00:31:03,404 --> 00:31:06,241
could be blessed
with a child of your own.

396
00:31:06,674 --> 00:31:07,608
Serena?

397
00:31:09,810 --> 00:31:12,413
-Praise be.
- Excuse me.

398
00:31:14,782 --> 00:31:17,218
The Driver will take you home.
You must be exhausted.

399
00:31:17,218 --> 00:31:18,586
I'm doing fine. Thank you.

400
00:31:18,586 --> 00:31:21,156
There's still so many people
here to greet and talk to.

401
00:31:21,156 --> 00:31:24,225
They're not here to see you.
They're here to see Noah.

402
00:31:24,225 --> 00:31:26,927
He is the star attraction.

403
00:31:26,927 --> 00:31:29,264
Leave Noah
here with us.

404
00:31:29,264 --> 00:31:33,468
Tomorrow, I think
I'll bring Noah by myself,

405
00:31:33,468 --> 00:31:35,203
so you can get some more rest.

406
00:31:35,203 --> 00:31:37,638
That sounds like
a pretty sweet deal to me.

407
00:31:43,344 --> 00:31:45,613
Right. I am quite tired.

408
00:31:47,815 --> 00:31:49,884
I'll just need to nurse him
before I leave.

409
00:31:49,884 --> 00:31:52,220
No need.
We'll just use a bottle.

410
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:54,589
I didn't bring one.

411
00:31:56,257 --> 00:31:58,326
I told you to always
have one on hand.

412
00:32:00,060 --> 00:32:03,097
I should have packed one,
Mrs. Wheeler.

413
00:32:03,097 --> 00:32:06,167
My mistake.
Just so foolish of me.

414
00:32:08,869 --> 00:32:12,473
Well, just don't take too long.

415
00:32:12,473 --> 00:32:15,776
Think that's
up to little Noah, isn't it?

416
00:32:20,047 --> 00:32:21,882
Thank you for letting me
be a part of today.

417
00:32:21,882 --> 00:32:24,352
I'm very grateful.

418
00:32:24,352 --> 00:32:27,422
There's a nice quiet spot
in the back, Mrs. Waterford.

419
00:32:27,422 --> 00:32:28,323
Thank you.

420
00:32:44,672 --> 00:32:46,641
Shh, shh.

421
00:33:08,629 --> 00:33:10,598
Do you mind
if I have some privacy?

422
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:13,801
Of course.

423
00:33:21,242 --> 00:33:22,443
Thank you so much.

424
00:33:52,106 --> 00:33:53,841
Please stop. Stop. Stop.

425
00:33:54,775 --> 00:33:57,445
Please. Please.

426
00:33:59,414 --> 00:34:01,349
Please stop. Stop, stop!

427
00:34:07,655 --> 00:34:10,658
Please. Please help me
save my son. Please.

428
00:34:11,492 --> 00:34:13,928
- Okay. Get in.
- Thank you.

429
00:34:18,198 --> 00:34:20,901
Thank you, bless you.
Please, just go. Please.

430
00:35:12,553 --> 00:35:13,854
Wish you'd said yes.

431
00:35:16,424 --> 00:35:18,859
- To Lawrence's offer?
- Yeah.

432
00:35:19,627 --> 00:35:22,296
Why didn't you say yes to Mark?

433
00:35:22,296 --> 00:35:24,465
He told me.

434
00:35:24,465 --> 00:35:27,267
He said he could still help you
come to Canada.

435
00:35:27,267 --> 00:35:30,405
Why the fuck
didn't you say anything?

436
00:35:30,405 --> 00:35:33,040
- I can't just pick up and leave.
- But you expect me to?

437
00:35:34,742 --> 00:35:39,580
- I'm married now. I have a Wife.
- I have Luke. I have Nichole.

438
00:35:39,580 --> 00:35:43,784
- You can bring Rose with you.
- No. Can't.

439
00:35:43,784 --> 00:35:46,353
Gilead's her home.

440
00:35:46,353 --> 00:35:48,489
Her father's the top Commander.
She's happy there.

441
00:35:48,489 --> 00:35:53,494
Happy? So what happens when
they want you to have a baby?

442
00:35:53,494 --> 00:35:56,096
What happens when they issue you
a Handmaid, and your Wife

443
00:35:56,096 --> 00:35:57,297
has to hold her down
while you--

444
00:35:57,297 --> 00:35:58,799
She's pregnant.

445
00:36:05,272 --> 00:36:06,541
Rose is pregnant.

446
00:36:11,078 --> 00:36:11,946
Oh.

447
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:20,588
Right.

448
00:36:24,559 --> 00:36:26,927
Gilead's changing.

449
00:36:26,927 --> 00:36:31,065
There's progress under Lawrence.
We're making it better.

450
00:36:34,368 --> 00:36:35,503
"We"?

451
00:36:37,972 --> 00:36:39,874
I have to do whatever it takes
to protect my family,

452
00:36:39,874 --> 00:36:41,075
just like you.

453
00:36:44,812 --> 00:36:46,914
I want what's best
for both our families.

454
00:37:00,961 --> 00:37:03,430
Well, this is
a fine mess, isn't it?

455
00:37:05,032 --> 00:37:06,634
And the world's a mess.

456
00:37:13,340 --> 00:37:15,910
Yeah. You know what
I wish, though?

457
00:37:18,779 --> 00:37:20,915
I wish the world
would just go away.

458
00:37:23,684 --> 00:37:24,952
Just for a little bit.

459
00:37:30,891 --> 00:37:32,893
It's gonna be hard for us
to see each other.

460
00:37:36,864 --> 00:37:38,699
I don't want
to make trouble for you.

461
00:37:46,974 --> 00:37:49,744
Do me a favor and tell Nichole
that I love her.

462
00:37:53,013 --> 00:37:55,249
Tell her I miss her and that
I think about her all the time.

463
00:37:55,249 --> 00:37:56,751
You do that for me?

464
00:37:57,652 --> 00:37:58,786
Of course I will.

465
00:38:04,859 --> 00:38:05,960
I should go.

466
00:38:08,529 --> 00:38:09,797
Enjoy yourself.

467
00:38:12,567 --> 00:38:15,536
Yeah. I haven't seen enough
of my own driver yet.

468
00:38:21,275 --> 00:38:22,209
I love you.

469
00:38:29,950 --> 00:38:30,985
I love you.

470
00:38:45,099 --> 00:38:46,767
- Hey, Nick?
- Yeah.

471
00:38:48,803 --> 00:38:51,071
Children look to their fathers,
you know.

472
00:38:52,940 --> 00:38:54,241
Set an example.

473
00:39:31,900 --> 00:39:33,902
Rose, I'm so happy for you.

474
00:39:33,902 --> 00:39:36,571
There's no greater gift
than a child.

475
00:39:36,571 --> 00:39:38,606
I know Agnes
has certainly been mine.

476
00:39:40,141 --> 00:39:44,913
Oh, glory be.
You are absolutely glowing.

477
00:39:45,613 --> 00:39:46,882
How lovely.

478
00:39:46,882 --> 00:39:49,450
Blessings upon you
and the Commander, Mrs. Blaine.

479
00:39:49,450 --> 00:39:50,652
Thank you, Aunt Lydia.

480
00:39:50,652 --> 00:39:52,688
Aunts are on the guest list now?

481
00:39:54,589 --> 00:39:56,725
Aunt Lydia's here
at the Commander's request.

482
00:39:58,727 --> 00:40:00,228
To be my chaperone.

483
00:40:00,228 --> 00:40:03,965
It is my honor
to accompany you, Mrs. Putnam.

484
00:40:05,466 --> 00:40:09,004
Well, thank the Lord
for such an incredible miracle.

485
00:40:09,004 --> 00:40:12,407
- You and Nick must be thrilled.
- And concerned.

486
00:40:14,175 --> 00:40:18,680
Chance for any genetic issues...
Considering.

487
00:40:22,350 --> 00:40:24,119
We'll leave that in God's hands.

488
00:40:30,425 --> 00:40:32,794
Brothers, the world knows now

489
00:40:32,794 --> 00:40:35,363
that Gilead
will defend its borders

490
00:40:36,364 --> 00:40:37,365
and protect our children.

491
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:40,836
And the force
and the fury of God,

492
00:40:40,836 --> 00:40:43,438
they kept my dear Agnes
and all the other girls safe.

493
00:40:44,172 --> 00:40:45,841
Praise be.

494
00:40:45,841 --> 00:40:49,110
Not to mention, we've
strengthened our alliances.

495
00:40:49,110 --> 00:40:52,180
The ambassadors from China,
Russia and North Korea

496
00:40:52,180 --> 00:40:54,482
have all congratulated us

497
00:40:54,482 --> 00:40:55,917
for sticking it
to the Americans.

498
00:40:55,917 --> 00:40:58,720
Well, I guess we're playing
with the big boys now.

499
00:40:58,720 --> 00:41:00,221
Yeah, what's the old saying?

500
00:41:00,221 --> 00:41:02,991
"Any club that would have me
as a member..."

501
00:41:08,563 --> 00:41:11,833
Blaine, our troops
are on the move?

502
00:41:11,833 --> 00:41:13,534
Yes, sir.
We'll have two battalions

503
00:41:13,534 --> 00:41:14,770
waiting at the border.

504
00:41:14,770 --> 00:41:16,104
Well, that's excellent.

505
00:41:16,104 --> 00:41:18,373
Canada will think twice
before letting the Americans

506
00:41:18,373 --> 00:41:20,241
use their airspace again.

507
00:41:20,241 --> 00:41:24,345
So all in all, a success.

508
00:41:24,345 --> 00:41:28,917
Well, June Osborne
is still stirring up trouble.

509
00:41:30,118 --> 00:41:33,154
It's about time we fixed
that problem. Don't you agree?

510
00:41:38,459 --> 00:41:43,298
Certainly worth considering.
Shall we, gentlemen?

511
00:41:55,076 --> 00:41:57,012
-  You okay?
- Now that you're here.

512
00:42:06,387 --> 00:42:08,056
May I take a moment

513
00:42:08,056 --> 00:42:10,125
to thank our gracious host?

514
00:42:11,860 --> 00:42:13,795
Your vision for Gilead's future,

515
00:42:13,795 --> 00:42:16,832
your commitment to our values
and our purpose.

516
00:42:18,399 --> 00:42:22,003
You have impressed, and, well,
surprised me, Commander.

517
00:42:27,075 --> 00:42:32,580
I like to defy expectations.

518
00:42:32,580 --> 00:42:34,015
I'd say you have.

519
00:42:35,583 --> 00:42:37,018
You're truly one of us now.

520
00:42:38,219 --> 00:42:39,554
Praise be.

521
00:42:41,489 --> 00:42:42,490
Praise be.

522
00:42:45,861 --> 00:42:48,629
Lieutenant
Miguel Rodriguez.

523
00:42:49,831 --> 00:42:51,867
Ensign Evan Sandler.

524
00:42:53,969 --> 00:42:56,237
Chief Petty Officer Levi Scott.

525
00:42:56,237 --> 00:42:58,139
Get out!
Go home!

526
00:42:58,139 --> 00:43:01,442
Senior Chief Petty Officer
Jill Strickland.

527
00:43:01,442 --> 00:43:02,543
Fuck America!

528
00:43:02,543 --> 00:43:04,145
They deserved it!

529
00:43:05,646 --> 00:43:07,949
Ensign Benjamin Turner.

530
00:43:08,984 --> 00:43:12,420
Petty Officer First Class
Adam Umansky.

531
00:43:12,420 --> 00:43:15,957
Go home!

532
00:43:15,957 --> 00:43:19,928
Commander Elijah...
Commander Elijah Vance.

533
00:43:21,829 --> 00:43:23,531
We remember these patriots.

534
00:43:27,468 --> 00:43:31,039
Their service. Their courage.

535
00:43:33,875 --> 00:43:35,210
Their sacrifice.

536
00:43:36,677 --> 00:43:37,845
For our country.

537
00:43:42,317 --> 00:43:44,285
And now, Emma?

538
00:43:58,399 --> 00:44:00,535
I pledge allegiance...

539
00:44:07,108 --> 00:44:10,278
Get the fuck
out of my country!

540
00:44:12,948 --> 00:44:15,016
I pledge...

541
00:44:16,918 --> 00:44:18,553
Can I help?

542
00:44:25,860 --> 00:44:29,130
Hi, Emma. Can I help you?

543
00:44:30,498 --> 00:44:33,601
Say it with me? Okay. Ready?

544
00:44:36,371 --> 00:44:40,275
"I pledge allegiance
to the Flag..."

545
00:44:41,509 --> 00:44:45,080
"Of the United States
of America...

546
00:44:46,481 --> 00:44:51,152
"and to the Republic
for which it stands..."

547
00:44:51,152 --> 00:44:56,157
"One nation under God,
indivisible..."

548
00:44:56,891 --> 00:44:59,627
"With liberty and justice...''

